1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:04,200
Hi, we're Hyeonmin and Jaewu, and this is DropPDF.

2
00:00:04,390 --> 00:00:06,400
It turns your files into PDFs,

3
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:11,160
and turns PDFs back into Word or PowerPoint, all right in your browser.

4
00:00:11,810 --> 00:00:16,060
There's nothing to install, and your files never leave your computer.

5
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:19,920
Let's start by dragging in a few files:

6
00:00:20,020 --> 00:00:22,600
a Word report, an Excel sheet,

7
00:00:22,739 --> 00:00:26,660
a ZIP full of trip photos, and a PDF brochure.

8
00:00:27,250 --> 00:00:30,510
Each row shows what the file will turn into.

9
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:35,050
Since the brochure is already a PDF, I get to choose what it becomes.

10
00:00:35,150 --> 00:00:39,720
It can be Word, PowerPoint, images, or a plain text file.

11
00:00:40,200 --> 00:00:44,310
If I only need one file, I can just click Convert on that row.

12
00:00:44,710 --> 00:00:46,990
In a moment, the report is saved,

13
00:00:47,110 --> 00:00:49,270
and here's the PDF it made.

14
00:00:49,720 --> 00:00:53,760
You can see the table and layout, just like the original.

15
00:00:54,360 --> 00:00:55,930
For everything else,

16
00:00:56,190 --> 00:00:58,310
you can click Convert all.

17
00:00:59,460 --> 00:01:05,319
So instead of four separate files, DropPDF puts every photo into one PDF,

18
00:01:05,420 --> 00:01:08,690
one page per photo, in the right order.

19
00:01:09,290 --> 00:01:11,750
The brochure is now a Word document.

20
00:01:12,040 --> 00:01:14,430
Here's a quick preview in the Library,

21
00:01:14,530 --> 00:01:17,120
and here it is open in Microsoft Word.

22
00:01:17,440 --> 00:01:19,240
It's not just a picture of the page.

23
00:01:19,340 --> 00:01:22,540
I can click into the heading and keep typing,

24
00:01:22,650 --> 00:01:26,000
while the photos and background stay right where they were.

25
00:01:26,700 --> 00:01:30,290
The same brochure can also become slides.

26
00:01:30,390 --> 00:01:35,770
I just switch the format to PowerPoint and hit Convert again,

27
00:01:35,870 --> 00:01:39,330
with no need to upload anything twice.

28
00:01:39,550 --> 00:01:43,450
And here's the brochure as a PowerPoint slide.

29
00:01:44,150 --> 00:01:51,220
Every result is saved in the Library, so it's still here even after I close the browser.

30
00:01:51,340 --> 00:01:54,710
I can search to find a file quickly,

31
00:01:54,810 --> 00:01:57,410
open a preview without downloading it,

32
00:01:57,510 --> 00:02:02,810
and rename a file or add a memo so I can remember what it's for.

33
00:02:03,410 --> 00:02:06,310
If I need another format later,

34
00:02:06,410 --> 00:02:09,710
Convert again sends the original back to the list,

35
00:02:09,810 --> 00:02:12,060
so I don't have to dig it up again.

36
00:02:12,330 --> 00:02:14,360
Anything I don't need is one click to delete,

37
00:02:14,460 --> 00:02:17,360
and Delete all clears the whole library.

38
00:02:18,050 --> 00:02:22,810
Okay, so that's DropPDF: drop in your files, pick a format,

39
00:02:22,910 --> 00:02:25,650
and keep everything organized in one place.

40
00:02:26,030 --> 00:02:28,210
We hope it saves you some time.

41
00:02:28,430 --> 00:02:30,020
Thank you for watching.

